  abstract={In this paper, a novel continuously tunable bandpass filter with a continuous tuning between single- and dual-passband responses is proposed. The filter consists of two parallel channels based on stepped-impedance resonators (SIRs) loaded with varactors. By adjusting the bias voltages of the varactors, the two passbands can either merge into a single passband or separate into two passbands. A prototype operating around 1.5 GHz was designed and measured. For the single-band response, the central frequencies are continuously tuned from 1.24 to 1.73 GHz, with 3-dB fractional bandwidths (FBWs) and insertion loss (IL)ranging from 7.2% to 10% and 3.47 dB to 3.67 dB, respectively. For the dual-band mode, the lower and upper passbands can be independently tuned from 1.28 to 1.58 GHz and 1.44 to 1.73 GHz, with FBWs of 4.4% - 8.9%.},
